# WARNING TO ANYONE ADDING GATE EVIDENCE HERE, AND TO ANY GATE THAT SEARCHES samples/:
#
# This directory records what a GATE PRINTED -- including the stale figures the round was
# fixing. That makes every previously-wrong figure permanently findable under samples/, so
# a gate asserting "this figure exists in an artefact" will PASS a stale figure on the
# strength of a file whose entire purpose is to record it as WRONG.
#
# Measured, not hypothetical: with this directory included in the search, both
# `spread=0.85s` and `sessions with any activity in 7d: 35` passed the figure gate while
# being the exact defects two review rounds blocked on.
#
# scripts/check_figures.sh therefore searches with --exclude-dir=gate-evidence. If you add
# another kind of evidence directory, exclude it too. An artefact of a FAILURE is not an
# artefact of a MEASUREMENT.
#
# This hazard was created by the artefact below, which a reviewer asked for in round 2 and
# which was worth having -- the exclusion is its price, noted here at the source rather
# than only at the gate.
